From: =?utf-8?q?Sebastian_Dr=C3=B6ge?= <sebastian@centricular.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Oct 2024 12:58:08 +0200
Subject: arcbox: Document that implementing weak references via the
 clear_func is not safe

Origin: upstream, 2.83.1, commit:dc197cd7f30bff718ea06fe6978c9ce203a40dc6
---
 glib/garcbox.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/glib/garcbox.c b/glib/garcbox.c
index da19cd4..400280c 100644
--- a/glib/garcbox.c
+++ b/glib/garcbox.c
@@ -207,6 +207,11 @@ g_atomic_rc_box_release (gpointer mem_block)
  * to clear the contents of @mem_block, and then will free the
  * resources allocated for @mem_block.
  *
+ * Note that implementing weak references via @clear_func is not thread-safe:
+ * clearing a pointer to the memory from the callback can race with another
+ * thread trying to access it as @mem_block already has a reference count of 0
+ * when the callback is called and will be freed.
+ *
  * Since: 2.58
  */
 void
